<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech govt approves 1997 balanced budget draft.</title>
<headline>Czech govt approves 1997 balanced budget draft.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Czech cabinet approved a draft proposal for a balanced state budget in 1997, with both revenues and expenditures totalling 549.1 billion crowns, Prime Minister Vaclav Klaus said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p> CZECH STATE BUDGET   FY 1997    FY 1996    FY 1995</p>
<p>  Revenues		 549.1	491.0	439.9</p>
<p>  Expenditures	   549.1	491.0	432.7</p>
<p>  Balance		    0.0	  0.0	  7.2</p>
<p>NOTE. All figures are in billions of crowns. The government recently approved some 9.3 billion crowns in expenditure cuts to arrive at the 1996 expenditure figure.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 42-2-2423-0003</p>
